---
/**
 * Real estate.
 *
 * GATED. While features.realEstate is false this page renders only the
 * blocked notice — none of the marketing copy exists in the output, and the
 * nav omits the link entirely. See the gate definition in content/idf.ts for
 * why. Do not open the gate without a Virginia real estate FIRM licence
 * number for the advertising entity.
 */
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import BlockedSlot from '../components/BlockedSlot.astro';
import { features } from '../content/idf';
---

<Page
  title="Real Estate — Interior Design Flooring"
  description="Real estate services page, pending licence verification."
  heading="Real estate"
  standfirst="This page is not cleared for publication."
  current="/real-estate/"
>
  <section class="hp-section hp-section--tight">
    {
      features.realEstate ? (
        <p>Real estate content goes here once the gate is opened.</p>
      ) : (
        <div class="fin-blocked">
          <BlockedSlot label="REAL ESTATE SERVICES — BLOCKED PENDING FIRM LICENCE VERIFICATION" />
          <p class="fin-blocked-note">
            Advertising brokerage services in Virginia requires the advertising entity to
            hold a real estate <strong>firm</strong> licence. Individual agents holding
            licences under another brokerage is not sufficient, and advertisements must
            carry the licensed brokerage name.
          </p>
          <p class="fin-blocked-note">
            The proposed renovation discount for clients who use the in-house realtor needs
            separate review: a thing of value offered in exchange for referring settlement
            service business can engage federal rules on affiliated business arrangements.
          </p>
          <p class="fin-blocked-note">
            Neither point is a design decision. Both need the firm licence number and, for
            the discount, a real estate attorney's sign-off before this page can exist.
          </p>
        </div>
      )
    }
  </section>
</Page>
